{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# POS Tagging and Syntactic Parsing Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: most-frequent-tag baseline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The dumbest POS tagger that works. For each word, predict the tag it had most often in training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from collections import Counter, defaultdict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_mft(train_examples):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    word_tag_counts = defaultdict(Counter)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    all_tags = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for tokens, tags in train_examples:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for token, tag in zip(tokens, tags):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            word_tag_counts[token.lower()][tag] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            all_tags[tag] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    word_best = {w: c.most_common(1)[0][0] for w, c in word_tag_counts.items()}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    default_tag = all_tags.most_common(1)[0][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return word_best, default_tag"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def predict_mft(tokens, word_best, default_tag):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [word_best.get(t.lower(), default_tag) for t in tokens]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "On the Brown corpus, this baseline hits ~85% accuracy. Not good, but the floor below which no serious model should fall."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: bigram HMM tagger"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Model the joint probability of the sequence:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "P(tags, words) = prod P(tag_i | tag_{i-1}) * P(word_i | tag_i)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two tables: transition probabilities (tag given previous tag), emission probabilities (word given tag). Estimate both from counts with Laplace smoothing. Decode with Viterbi (dynamic programming over the tag lattice)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_hmm(train_examples, alpha=0.01):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    transitions = defaultdict(Counter)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    emissions = defaultdict(Counter)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tags = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vocab = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for tokens, ts in train_examples:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prev = \"<BOS>\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for token, tag in zip(tokens, ts):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            transitions[prev][tag] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            emissions[tag][token.lower()] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tags.add(tag)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            vocab.add(token.lower())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            prev = tag"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        transitions[prev][\"<EOS>\"] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return transitions, emissions, tags, vocab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def log_prob(table, given, key, smooth_denom, alpha):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return math.log((table[given].get(key, 0) + alpha) / smooth_denom)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def viterbi(tokens, transitions, emissions, tags, vocab, alpha=0.01):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tags_list = list(tags)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    V = [[0.0] * len(tags_list) for _ in range(n)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    back = [[0] * len(tags_list) for _ in range(n)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for j, tag in enumerate(tags_list):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        em_denom = sum(emissions[tag].values()) + alpha * (len(vocab) + 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tr_denom = sum(transitions[\"<BOS>\"].values()) + alpha * (len(tags_list) + 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tr = log_prob(transitions, \"<BOS>\", tag, tr_denom, alpha)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        em = log_prob(emissions, tag, tokens[0].lower(), em_denom, alpha)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        V[0][j] = tr + em"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        back[0][j] = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(1, n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j, tag in enumerate(tags_list):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            em_denom = sum(emissions[tag].values()) + alpha * (len(vocab) + 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            em = log_prob(emissions, tag, tokens[i].lower(), em_denom, alpha)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best_prev = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best_score = -1e30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for k, prev_tag in enumerate(tags_list):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                tr_denom = sum(transitions[prev_tag].values()) + alpha * (len(tags_list) + 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                tr = log_prob(transitions, prev_tag, tag, tr_denom, alpha)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                score = V[i - 1][k] + tr + em"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if score > best_score:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    best_score = score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    best_prev = k"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            V[i][j] = best_score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            back[i][j] = best_prev"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    last_best = max(range(len(tags_list)), key=lambda j: V[n - 1][j])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    path = [last_best]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        path.append(back[i][path[-1]])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [tags_list[j] for j in reversed(path)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Bigram HMM on Brown hits ~93% accuracy. The jump from 85% to 93% is mostly transition probabilities \u2014 the model learns `DET NOUN` is common and `NOUN DET` is rare."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: why modern taggers beat this"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Transition + emission probabilities are local. They cannot capture that `saw` is a noun in \"I bought a saw\" but a verb in \"I saw the movie.\" A CRF with arbitrary features (suffix, word shape, word before and after, word itself) hits ~97%. A BiLSTM-CRF or transformer hits ~98%+."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The ceiling on this task is set by annotator disagreement. Human annotators agree about 97% of the time on Penn Treebank. Models past 98% are probably overfitting the test set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: dependency parsing sketch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Full dependency parsing from scratch is out of scope; the canonical textbook treatment is in Jurafsky and Martin. Two classical families to know:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Transition-based** parsers (arc-eager, arc-standard) act like a shift-reduce parser: they read tokens, shift them onto a stack, and apply reduce actions that create arcs. Greedy decoding is fast. Classic implementation is MaltParser. Modern neural version: Chen and Manning's transition-based parser."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Graph-based** parsers (Eisner's algorithm, Dozat-Manning biaffine) score every possible head-dependent edge and pick the maximum spanning tree. Slower but more accurate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For most applied work, call spaCy:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import spacy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nlp = spacy.load(\"en_core_web_sm\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "doc = nlp(\"The cats were running at 3pm.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for token in doc:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{token.text:10s} tag={token.tag_:5s} pos={token.pos_:6s} dep={token.dep_:10s} head={token.head.text}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The        tag=DT    pos=DET    dep=det        head=cats"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "cats       tag=NNS   pos=NOUN   dep=nsubj      head=running"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "were       tag=VBD   pos=AUX    dep=aux        head=running"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "running    tag=VBG   pos=VERB   dep=ROOT       head=running"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "at         tag=IN    pos=ADP    dep=prep       head=running"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3pm        tag=NN    pos=NOUN   dep=pobj       head=at"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ".          tag=.     pos=PUNCT  dep=punct      head=running"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Read the `dep` column bottom to top and the sentence's grammatical structure falls out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Using the most-frequent-tag baseline on a small tagged corpus (e.g., NLTK's Brown subset), measure accuracy on held-out sentences. Verify the ~85% result.\n2. **Medium.** Train the bigram HMM above and report per-tag precision/recall. Which tags does the HMM confuse most?\n3. **Hard.** Use spaCy's dependency parse to extract subject-verb-object triples from a 1000-sentence sample. Evaluate on 50 manually labeled triples. Document where extraction fails (often passives, coordinations, and elided subjects)."
      ]
    }
